  "lean": {
    "statement": "∀ {E : Type u_1} [inst : NormedAddCommGroup E] [inst_1 : InnerProductSpace ℝ E] [inst_2 : CompleteSpace E]\n  [FiniteDimensional ℝ E] [inst_4 : MeasurableSpace E] [BorelSpace E] {U : E → ℝ} {m b : NNReal},\n  ContDiff ℝ 2 U →\n    (∀ (x v : E), ↑m * ‖v‖ ^ 2 ≤ ((fderiv ℝ (fderiv ℝ U) x) v) v ∧ ((fderiv ℝ (fderiv ℝ U) x) v) v ≤ ↑b * ‖v‖ ^ 2) →\n      m ≤ b →\n        ∀ {A d : ℝ},\n          0 < A →\n            0 < d →\n              d = ↑(Module.finrank ℝ E) →\n                ∀ (u : E),\n                  have F := fun x => U x + A⁻¹ / 2 * ‖x - u‖ ^ 2;\n                  have a := ↑m + A⁻¹;\n                  have c := ↑b + A⁻¹;\n                  have k := c / a;\n                  have T := fun x => x - c⁻¹ • gradient F x;\n                  have N := fun v => if h : ∃ n, ‖gradient F (T^[n] v)‖ ^ 2 ≤ d / A then Nat.find h else 0;\n                  have xp := fun v => T^[N v] v;\n                  0 < a ∧\n                    0 < c ∧\n                      1 ≤ k ∧\n                        (∀ (x : E), gradient F x = gradient U x + A⁻¹ • (x - u)) ∧\n                          Measurable N ∧\n                            Measurable xp ∧\n                              (∀ (v : E),\n                                  ‖gradient F (xp v)‖ ^ 2 ≤ d / A ∧\n                                    ‖u - A • gradient U (xp v) - xp v‖ = A * ‖gradient F (xp v)‖ ∧\n                                      ‖u - A • gradient U (xp v) - xp v‖ ≤ √(d * A) ∧\n                                        (∀ j < N v, d / A < ‖gradient F (T^[j] v)‖ ^ 2) ∧\n                                          N v ≤ ⌈k * Real.log (1 + A * ‖gradient F v‖ ^ 2 / d)⌉₊ ∧\n                                            ↑(N v) + 1 ≤ k * Real.log (1 + A * ‖gradient F v‖ ^ 2 / d) + 2) ∧\n                                ∀ (μ : MeasureTheory.Measure E),\n                                  MeasureTheory.IsProbabilityMeasure μ →\n                                    ∀ (M : ℝ),\n                                      MeasureTheory.Integrable (fun v => ‖gradient F v‖ ^ 2) μ →\n                                        ∫ (v : E), ‖gradient F v‖ ^ 2 ∂μ ≤ M →\n                                          MeasureTheory.Integrable (fun v => ↑(N v) + 1) μ ∧\n                                            ∫ (v : E), ↑(N v) + 1 ∂μ ≤ 2 + k * Real.log (1 + A * M / d)",
    "statement_sha256": "3eb914a674746149f984ac3ec853ffd112108e16c2a3f42a3a864adb4c7fbc0a",
    "compiled": true,
    "approved_definition_context": [
      "NNReal is the type of nonnegative real numbers; the upward arrow denotes the displayed type coercion. Module.finrank is finite real vector-space dimension.",
      "ContDiff R 2 means twice continuously differentiable. fderiv R is the actual Frechet derivative; (fderiv R (fderiv R U) x v) v evaluates its second derivative on (v,v). gradient is the actual real inner-product gradient. The dot-shaped scalar operation denotes scalar multiplication.",
      "T^[n] v is the n-fold iterate of T at v, including T^[0] v=v. Nat.find returns the least natural satisfying its supplied existence proof. The dependent conditional has the displayed zero fallback. Natural ceiling is the least nonnegative integer at least its real argument.",
      "Measurable refers to the displayed sigma-algebras; BorelSpace identifies the state sigma-algebra with its topology. IsProbabilityMeasure mu says mu has total mass one. Integrable means actual Bochner integrability, and the real integral is the Bochner integral.",
      "All local definitions have been expanded from the compiled theorem type and checked by Meta.isDefEq. The displayed let-bound functions retain their scopes. No source or algorithm identity is supplied."
    ]
